  "note": "The `why:'ready'` limb of the hand-back wait, MEASURED 2026-11-26 (dev-handback-ready 1795738550085): the native edge serves init + two segments and then refuses native media until 25.4 s, so the midroll (10-24 s) starves the element below HAVE_FUTURE_DATA and the wait arms at rs=2 (`handback-wait {ms:24551, rs:2}`); the edge RESUMES 0.85 s after the pod end and the element reaches rs=4, so the wait exits at 907 ms with `handback-ready {capped:false, rs:4, why:'ready'}` instead of hitting the 3000 ms ceiling. dev-handback-wait keeps the `why:'cap'` limb (its edge refuses for 30 s). The pixel/cover arms live there: with a 907 ms window, fixed sample instants cannot fall inside it, and an arm that grades the wrong instants is a defect of the arm."
